IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `snap-core`
IMPORT `snap1-logic`
IMPORT `snap1-s2014-abc`

-- 7 U.S.C. 2014(e)(1) to (5): the standard, earned income, dependent care, child support and excess medical expense deductions.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- COMPOSITION RULE (assumed, not ruled): an AMOUNT function is arithmetic given that the household is entitled; an ENTITLEMENT function answers
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE / NOTHING. A deduction enters the net income of `snap1-s2014-e2` only when its entitlement function answers JUST TRUE,
-- and a household that is not shown to be entitled deducts nothing (that is arithmetic, not an answer to "is the household entitled?").
-- Seam taken as an input: s 2012(j) (the household includes an elderly or disabled member).

§ `s 2014(e)(1) Standard deduction`

-- Standard deductions, FY 2027 (USDA Table 2, lines 74-81 of inputs/fna-snap-cola-fy2027.txt).
-- The row marked 6 is the row for 6 OR MORE members (the USDA's "6+"); the rows for 1, 2 and 3 members are equal.
-- Columns, in the core's order: the 48 States and DC, Alaska urban, rural 1, rural 2, Guam, Hawaii, the Virgin Islands (Alaska repeated across its three).
`s 2014(e)(1) standard deductions, FY 2027` MEANS `Annual table` WITH
    `fiscal year`    IS 2027
    `what it states` IS "FY 2027 standard deductions, in dollars a month (USDA Table 2); the row marked 6 is for 6 or more members"
    `the rows`       IS LIST
        (`Table row` OF 1, (`Dollars by area` OF 217, 371, 371, 371, 435, 306, 191))
      , (`Table row` OF 2, (`Dollars by area` OF 217, 371, 371, 371, 435, 306, 191))
      , (`Table row` OF 3, (`Dollars by area` OF 217, 371, 371, 371, 435, 306, 191))
      , (`Table row` OF 4, (`Dollars by area` OF 229, 371, 371, 371, 457, 306, 229))
      , (`Table row` OF 5, (`Dollars by area` OF 268, 371, 371, 371, 536, 309, 268))
      , (`Table row` OF 6, (`Dollars by area` OF 308, 385, 385, 385, 614, 354, 308))

-- src:252 | (1) Standard deduction
-- src:253 | (A) In general
-- src:254 | (i) Deduction
-- src:255 | The Secretary shall allow a standard deduction for each household in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, and the Virgin Islands of the United States in an amount that is—
-- src:256 | (I) equal to 8.31 percent of the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1); but
-- src:257 | (II) not more than 8.31 percent of the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for a household of 6 members.
-- src:258 | (ii) Minimum amount
-- src:259 | Notwithstanding clause (i), the standard deduction for each household in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, and the Virgin Islands of the United States shall be not less than—
-- src:260 | (I) for fiscal year 2009, $144, $246, $203, and $127, respectively; and
-- src:261 | (II) for fiscal year 2010 and each fiscal year thereafter, an amount that is equal to the amount from the previous fiscal year adjusted to the nearest lower dollar increment to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor, for items other than food.
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(A), the formula and the floor (src:252-261)
GIVEN `the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for the household` IS A NUMBER
      `the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for a household of 6 members` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum amount under clause (ii)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(1)(A) the standard deduction` MEANS
    maximum (LIST `the minimum amount under clause (ii)`, minimum (LIST (8.31% TIMES `the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for the household`), (8.31% TIMES `the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for a household of 6 members`)))

-- src:262 | (B) Guam
-- src:263 | (i) In general
-- src:264 | The Secretary shall allow a standard deduction for each household in Guam in an amount that is—
-- src:265 | (I) equal to 8.31 percent of twice the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia; but
-- src:266 | (II) not more than 8.31 percent of twice the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia for a household of 6 members.
-- src:267 | (ii) Minimum amount
-- src:268 | Notwithstanding clause (i), the standard deduction for each household in Guam shall be not less than—
-- src:269 | (I) for fiscal year 2009, $289; and
-- src:270 | (II) for fiscal year 2010 and each fiscal year thereafter, an amount that is equal to the amount from the previous fiscal year adjusted to the nearest lower dollar increment to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor, for items other than food.
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(B), Guam (src:262-270)
GIVEN `the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia for the household` IS A NUMBER
      `the same standard for a household of 6 members` IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum amount under clause (ii)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(1)(B) the standard deduction for Guam` MEANS
    maximum (LIST `the minimum amount under clause (ii)`, minimum (LIST (8.31% TIMES (2 TIMES `the income standard of eligibility established under subsection (c)(1) for the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia for the household`)), (8.31% TIMES (2 TIMES `the same standard for a household of 6 members`))))

-- src:259 | Notwithstanding clause (i), the standard deduction for each household in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, and the Virgin Islands of the United States shall be not less than—
-- src:260 | (I) for fiscal year 2009, $144, $246, $203, and $127, respectively; and
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I), the floor for fiscal year 2009 (src:259-260)
GIVEN area IS AN Area
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for fiscal year 2009` MEANS
    CONSIDER area
        WHEN `the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia` THEN JUST 144
        WHEN `Alaska, urban` THEN JUST 246
        WHEN `Alaska, rural 1` THEN JUST 246
        WHEN `Alaska, rural 2` THEN JUST 246
        WHEN Hawaii THEN JUST 203
        WHEN `the Virgin Islands of the United States` THEN JUST 127
        WHEN Guam THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): clause (A)(ii)(I) names "the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, and the Virgin Islands"; Guam's floor is in subparagraph (B)(ii)(I)

-- src:267 | (ii) Minimum amount
-- src:268 | Notwithstanding clause (i), the standard deduction for each household in Guam shall be not less than—
-- src:269 | (I) for fiscal year 2009, $289; and
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(B)(ii)(I), the Guam floor for fiscal year 2009 (src:267-269)
`s 2014(e)(1)(B)(ii)(I) the minimum standard deduction for Guam for fiscal year 2009` MEANS 289

-- src:261 | an amount that is equal to the amount from the previous fiscal year adjusted to the nearest lower dollar increment to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor, for items other than food.
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(II), the floor after fiscal year 2009 (src:261)
GIVEN `the unrounded amount from the previous fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the change for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for items other than food, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(1)(A)(ii)(II) the minimum standard deduction after indexing` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the unrounded amount from the previous fiscal year, in dollars` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for items other than food, as a fraction`))

-- src:270 | an amount that is equal to the amount from the previous fiscal year adjusted to the nearest lower dollar increment to reflect changes for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers published by the Bureau of Labor Statistics of the Department of Labor, for items other than food.
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(B)(ii)(II), the Guam floor after fiscal year 2009 (src:270)
GIVEN `the unrounded amount from the previous fiscal year, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the change for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for items other than food, as a fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(1)(B)(ii)(II) the Guam minimum standard deduction after indexing` MEANS
    FLOOR (`the unrounded amount from the previous fiscal year, in dollars` TIMES (1 PLUS `the change for the 12-month period ending on the preceding June 30 in the Consumer Price Index for All Urban Consumers for items other than food, as a fraction`))

-- src:272 | Each adjustment under subparagraphs (A)(ii)(II) and (B)(ii)(II) shall be based on the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period.
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(C), requirement (src:272)
GIVEN `the adjustment was computed from the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(1)(C) the adjustment conforms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the adjustment was computed from the unrounded amount for the prior 12-month period` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be based on the unrounded amount"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text requires the unrounded base and does not say what follows from a rounded one

-- The standard deduction for a household, from the USDA's FY 2027 table: 6 or more members take the row marked 6; fewer than 1 member has no row.
-- src:255 | The Secretary shall allow a standard deduction for each household in the 48 contiguous States and the District of Columbia, Alaska, Hawaii, and the Virgin Islands of the United States in an amount that is—
@ref s 2014(e)(1)(A)(i), the deduction for each household (src:255)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      area IS AN Area
      size IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(1) the standard deduction for the household` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the fiscal year` EQUALS 2027) THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): only the fiscal year 2027 figures were supplied; the floor is indexed every year by the Consumer Price Index
        IF size LESS THAN 1 THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a household of fewer than 1 member has no row
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `household size` EQUALS (minimum (LIST size, 6))) (`s 2014(e)(1) standard deductions, FY 2027`'s `the rows`)
                WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
                WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (`s 2014(c) the figure for the area` (r's `the dollars`) area)

§ `s 2014(e)(2) Earned income deduction`

-- src:273 | (2) Earned income deduction
-- src:274 | (A) “Earned income” defined
-- src:275 | In this paragraph, the term “earned income” does not include—
-- src:276 | (i) income excluded by subsection (d); or
-- src:277 | (ii) any portion of income earned under a work supplementation or support program, as defined under section 2025(b) of this title, that is attributable to public assistance.
@ref s 2014(e)(2)(A), "earned income" defined (src:273-277)
GIVEN `the earned income remaining after the exclusions of subsection (d), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the portion of income earned under a work supplementation or support program, as defined under section 2025(b), that is attributable to public assistance, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(2)(A) the earned income` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, `the earned income remaining after the exclusions of subsection (d), in dollars` MINUS `the portion of income earned under a work supplementation or support program, as defined under section 2025(b), that is attributable to public assistance, in dollars`)

-- src:278 | (B) Deduction
-- src:279 | Except as provided in subparagraph (C), a household with earned income shall be allowed a deduction of 20 percent of all earned income to compensate for taxes, other mandatory deductions from salary, and work expenses.
-- src:280 | (C) Exception
-- src:281 | The deduction described in subparagraph (B) shall not be allowed with respect to determining an overissuance due to the failure of a household to report earned income in a timely manner.
@ref s 2014(e)(2)(B) and (C), the deduction and its exception (src:278-281)
GIVEN `the household's earned income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the question is an overissuance due to the failure of the household to report earned income in a timely manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(2) the household is allowed the earned income deduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the question is an overissuance due to the failure of the household to report earned income in a timely manner`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The deduction described in subparagraph (B) shall not be allowed with respect to determining an overissuance due to the failure of a household to report earned income in a timely manner"
        IF `the household's earned income, in dollars` GREATER THAN 0
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "a household with earned income shall be allowed a deduction of 20 percent of all earned income"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2)(B) reaches "a household with earned income"

-- src:279 | Except as provided in subparagraph (C), a household with earned income shall be allowed a deduction of 20 percent of all earned income to compensate for taxes, other mandatory deductions from salary, and work expenses.
@ref s 2014(e)(2)(B), the amount (src:279)
GIVEN `the household's earned income, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(2)(B) the earned income deduction` MEANS 20% TIMES `the household's earned income, in dollars`

§ `s 2014(e)(3) Dependent care deduction`

-- src:283 | (A) In general
-- src:284 | A household shall be entitled, with respect to expenses (other than excluded expenses described in subparagraph (B)) for dependent care, to a dependent care deduction for the actual cost of payments necessary for the care of a dependent if the care enables a household member to accept or continue employment, or training or education that is preparatory for employment.
@ref s 2014(e)(3)(A), the entitlement (src:283-284)
GIVEN `the payments are necessary for the care of a dependent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the care enables a household member to accept or continue employment, or training or education that is preparatory for employment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the household is entitled to the dependent care deduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the payments are necessary for the care of a dependent` AND `the care enables a household member to accept or continue employment, or training or education that is preparatory for employment`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "A household shall be entitled ... to a dependent care deduction for the actual cost of payments necessary for the care of a dependent if the care enables a household member to accept or continue employment"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the entitlement is "if the care enables a household member to accept or continue employment, or training or education that is preparatory for employment" (a failed "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:285 | (B) Excluded expenses
-- src:286 | The excluded expenses referred to in subparagraph (A) are—
-- src:287 | (i) expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party;
-- src:288 | (ii) amounts made available and excluded, for the expenses referred to in subparagraph (A), under subsection (d)(3); and
-- src:289 | (iii) expenses that are paid under section 2015(d)(4) of this title or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F) of this title.
@ref s 2014(e)(3)(B), the excluded expenses (src:285-289)
GIVEN `the expense is paid on behalf of the household by a third party` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expense is covered by amounts made available and excluded under subsection (d)(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the expense is paid under section 2015(d)(4) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(3)(B) the expense is an excluded expense` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the expense is paid on behalf of the household by a third party` OR `the expense is covered by amounts made available and excluded under subsection (d)(3)` OR `the expense is paid under section 2015(d)(4) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F)`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "The excluded expenses referred to in subparagraph (A) are— (i) ... (ii) ... (iii)"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The excluded expenses referred to in subparagraph (A) are" the three listed, a definition

-- src:283 | (A) In general
-- src:284 | A household shall be entitled, with respect to expenses (other than excluded expenses described in subparagraph (B)) for dependent care, to a dependent care deduction for the actual cost of payments necessary for the care of a dependent if the care enables a household member to accept or continue employment, or training or education that is preparatory for employment.
@ref s 2014(e)(3)(A), the amount (src:283-284)
GIVEN `the actual cost of the payments necessary for the care of the dependent, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the amounts made available and excluded under subsection (d)(3) for those expenses, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the expenses paid under section 2015(d)(4) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F), in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(3)(A) the dependent care deduction` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, `the actual cost of the payments necessary for the care of the dependent, in dollars` MINUS (`the expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, in dollars` PLUS `the amounts made available and excluded under subsection (d)(3) for those expenses, in dollars` PLUS `the expenses paid under section 2015(d)(4) or a pilot project under section 2025(h)(1)(F), in dollars`))

§ `s 2014(e)(4) Deduction for child support payments`

-- src:291 | (A) In general
-- src:292 | In lieu of providing an exclusion for legally obligated child support payments made by a household member under subsection (d)(6), a State agency may elect to provide a deduction for the amount of the payments.
@ref s 2014(e)(4)(A), the State agency's election (src:291-292)
GIVEN `the State agency has elected to provide a deduction for legally obligated child support payments` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the legally obligated child support payments made by a household member, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(4)(A) the child support deduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the State agency has elected to provide a deduction for legally obligated child support payments`
            THEN JUST `the legally obligated child support payments made by a household member, in dollars`  -- the text says yes: "a State agency may elect to provide a deduction for the amount of the payments"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deduction exists only "in lieu of providing an exclusion" where the State agency "may elect"; without the election paragraph (d)(6) governs

-- src:293 | (B) Order of determining deductions
-- src:294 | A deduction under this paragraph shall be determined before the computation of the excess shelter expense deduction under paragraph (6).
@ref s 2014(e)(4)(B), the order of determining deductions (src:293-294)
GIVEN `the position at which the child support deduction is determined` IS A NUMBER
      `the position at which the excess shelter expense deduction is computed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(4)(B) the order of the computations conforms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the position at which the child support deduction is determined` LESS THAN `the position at which the excess shelter expense deduction is computed`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "shall be determined before the computation of the excess shelter expense deduction"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A deduction under this paragraph shall be determined before the computation of the excess shelter expense deduction under paragraph (6)"

§ `s 2014(e)(5) Excess medical expense deduction`

-- src:296 | (A) In general
-- src:297 | A household containing an elderly or disabled member shall be entitled, with respect to expenses other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, to an excess medical expense deduction for the portion of the actual costs of allowable medical expenses, incurred by the elderly or disabled member, exclusive of special diets, that exceeds $35 per month.
@ref s 2014(e)(5)(A), the entitlement (src:296-297)
GIVEN `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(5)(A) the household is entitled to the excess medical expense deduction` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "A household containing an elderly or disabled member shall be entitled ... to an excess medical expense deduction"
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2012(j) the household includes an elderly or disabled member`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the entitlement is given to "A household containing an elderly or disabled member"; the text does not say what a household without one may deduct
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the household includes an elderly or disabled member (section 2012(j)) was not supplied

-- src:296 | (A) In general
-- src:297 | A household containing an elderly or disabled member shall be entitled, with respect to expenses other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party, to an excess medical expense deduction for the portion of the actual costs of allowable medical expenses, incurred by the elderly or disabled member, exclusive of special diets, that exceeds $35 per month.
@ref s 2014(e)(5)(A), the amount (src:296-297)
GIVEN `the actual costs of allowable medical expenses incurred by the elderly or disabled member, other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party and exclusive of special diets, in dollars a month` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2014(e)(5)(A) the excess medical expense deduction` MEANS
    maximum (LIST 0, `the actual costs of allowable medical expenses incurred by the elderly or disabled member, other than expenses paid on behalf of the household by a third party and exclusive of special diets, in dollars a month` MINUS 35)

-- src:298 | (B) Method of claiming deduction
-- src:299 | (i) In general
-- src:300 | A State agency shall offer an eligible household under subparagraph (A) a method of claiming a deduction for recurring medical expenses that are initially verified under the excess medical expense deduction in lieu of submitting information on, or verification of, actual expenses on a monthly basis.
@ref s 2014(e)(5)(B)(i), the method of claiming (src:298-300)
GIVEN `the household is an eligible household under subparagraph (A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(5)(B)(i) the State agency must offer the method of claiming recurring medical expenses` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the household is an eligible household under subparagraph (A)` THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "A State agency shall offer an eligible household under subparagraph (A) a method of claiming a deduction for recurring medical expenses"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty is owed to "an eligible household under subparagraph (A)"

-- src:301 | (ii) Method
-- src:302 | The method described in clause (i) shall—
-- src:303 | (I) be designed to minimize the burden for the eligible elderly or disabled household member choosing to deduct the recurrent medical expenses of the member pursuant to the method;
-- src:304 | (II) rely on reasonable estimates of the expected medical expenses of the member for the certification period (including changes that can be reasonably anticipated based on available information about the medical condition of the member, public or private medical insurance coverage, and the current verified medical expenses incurred by the member); and
-- src:305 | (III) not require further reporting or verification of a change in medical expenses if such a change has been anticipated for the certification period.
@ref s 2014(e)(5)(B)(ii), what the method shall do (src:301-305)
GIVEN `the method is designed to minimize the burden for the eligible elderly or disabled household member` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the method relies on reasonable estimates of the expected medical expenses of the member for the certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the method does not require further reporting or verification of a change in medical expenses that has been anticipated for the certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(5)(B)(ii) the method conforms` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the method is designed to minimize the burden for the eligible elderly or disabled household member` AND `the method relies on reasonable estimates of the expected medical expenses of the member for the certification period` AND `the method does not require further reporting or verification of a change in medical expenses that has been anticipated for the certification period`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: the method "shall— (I) be designed to minimize the burden ...; (II) rely on reasonable estimates ...; and (III) not require further reporting or verification"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text says what the method shall do and not what follows from a method that does not

-- src:305 | (III) not require further reporting or verification of a change in medical expenses if such a change has been anticipated for the certification period.
@ref s 2014(e)(5)(B)(ii)(III) (src:305)
GIVEN `the change in medical expenses has been anticipated for the certification period` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(5)(B)(ii)(III) further reporting or verification of the change may be required` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the change in medical expenses has been anticipated for the certification period`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the method shall "not require further reporting or verification of a change in medical expenses if such a change has been anticipated for the certification period"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a change "anticipated for the certification period"; the text is silent on any other change

-- src:306 | (C) Exclusion of medical marijuana
-- src:307 | The Secretary shall promulgate rules to ensure that medical marijuana is not treated as a medical expense for purposes of this paragraph.
@ref s 2014(e)(5)(C), medical marijuana (src:306-307)
GIVEN `the expense is for medical marijuana` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2014(e)(5)(C) the expense is treated as a medical expense` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the expense is for medical marijuana`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "medical marijuana is not treated as a medical expense for purposes of this paragraph"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (C) names medical marijuana only; whether another expense is a medical expense is for section 2012(c)
